      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the area of Mateen's backyard, we need to determine the dimensions of the rectangular backyard. We know that walking the length 25 times equals 1000 meters, and walking the perimeter 10 times also equals 1000 meters. Let's denote the length of the backyard by \\( L \\) and the width by \\( W \\).\n\nFirst, we express the circumference of one walk around the backyard (perimeter) in terms of \\( L \\) and \\( W \\):\n\n\\[\n2L + 2W = \\text{perimeter}\n\\]\n\nWe are given that walking the perimeter 10 times is equal to 1000 meters, so:\n\n\\[\n10L + 10W = 1000\n\\]\n\nSimplifying this equation, we get:\n\n\\[\nL + W = 100\n\\]\n\nNext, we express the length walked if he walks the length 25 times in terms of \\( L \\):\n\n\\[\n25L = 1000\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( L \\):\n\n\\[\nL = \\frac{1000}{25} = 40\n\\]\n\nSubstituting \\( L = 40 \\) back into the equation \\( L + W = 100 \\):\n\n\\[\n40 + W = 100\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\( W \\):\n\n\\[\nW = 100 - 40 = 60\n\\]\n\nNow we have the dimensions of the backyard:\n- Length \\( L = 40 \\) meters\n- Width \\( W = 60 \\) meters\n\nTo find the area \\( A \\) of the backyard, we multiply the length by the width:\n\n\\[\nA = L \\times W = 40 \\times 60 = 2400 \\text{ square meters}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of Mateen's backyard is \\(\\boxed{2400}\\) square meters.",
